# The generated string tables are UTF-16LE with a BOM, the encoding rc.exe
# reads as Unicode without a #pragma code_page (Localization/build.ps1).
# Line-ending normalisation corrupts them: a newline is 0D 00 0A 00, whose 0A
# reads as a lone LF, and checkout rewrites it to 0D 00 0D 0A 00 — one byte too
# many, and every code unit after it is misaligned.
#
# Git already infers this from the NUL bytes. Saying it means a later
# `* text=auto` cannot quietly undo it, since an explicit attribute wins over
# auto-detection.
src/DeskTick/Localization/*.rc binary
